>> title: Kibbeh
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: lamb, bulgur, lebanese, deep-fry, pine nuts, stuffed
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: kibbeh, kibbe, kibbie, kibbi, kubba, kubbeh, quibe, kibbeh makliyeh, fried kibbeh, kibbeh balls, torpedoes
>> pairs-with: labneh, tahini-sauce, kabis
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the filling goes in cold: a warm one steams inside the shell and blows it apart in the oil, taking the batch with it

>> step: soak the fine bulgur 30 min, squeeze dry
Cover @fine bulgur{1 1/2%cups}(250 g; #1 grade, the dust-fine one) in cold water and ~soak{30%min}, then wring it out in a cloth until it stops dripping.

>> step: fry the filling, 8 min, then cool
Fry @ground lamb{1/2%lb}(225 g), @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced fine), @pine nuts{1/3%cup}(45 g), @ground allspice{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} in @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a #skillet{} ~fry{8%min}, until the meat browns and the nuts colour, then ~cool{20%min} completely.

>> step: grind the shell to a paste
Grind @&(~2)squeezed bulgur{} with @lean ground lamb{1%lb}(450 g; leg, trimmed of all fat), @yellow onion{1%small}(quartered), @ground allspice{1%tsp}, @dried mint{1%tsp} and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} in a #food processor{} in batches until it is a smooth, tacky, uniform paste, adding a tablespoon of ice water if it stiffens.

>> step: shape torpedoes, chill 30 min
Shape @&(~1)kibbeh paste{} into egg-sized ovals with wet hands, hollow each around a finger into a thin shell, spoon in @&(~2)cooled filling{}, seal it to a point at each end, then ~chill{30%min}.

>> step: fry at 350°F 5 min
Fry @&(~1)shaped kibbeh{} in @neutral oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; at 350°F/175°C) four at a time ~fry{5%min}, until they are mahogany and float.
